      ],
      "helpful_votes": 1,
      "verified": false,
      "is_renewed": false,
      "source_url": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07J9LLTP7",
      "bm25_score": 5.458283424377441,
      "bm25_rank": 99,
      "dense_score": 0.7156974077224731,
      "dense_rank": 2,
      "aspect_boosted": true,
      "rrf_score": 0.022418340434165143,
      "rrf_normalized": 0.6837593832420369
    },
    {
      "rank": 17,
      "row_id": 369061,
      "chunk_id": "65f9fd8ed2fe_0",
      "doc_id": "65f9fd8ed2fe",
      "text": "Limited life. My experience is that you have to buy a new one of these every year or two. Presumably people turn in their phones when the battery starts to die out, and then that's what you are buying when you're the next owner. 15 months after purchase, my phone is dead during the time it takes to prepare for, get to and eat dinner out. So I carry an external battery everywhere, enjoy the bargain price, and investigate what phone besides this one I'll ask for during Christmas. Also for the record, this is from my earlier review: Thank heavens for the Amazon product support team, because I thought my phone was broken when it's not. They explained that sometimes Google Pixels screens flash with a flickering, sometimes strobe-light effect, and you have to stop what you are doing, go into Settings, and adjust brightness.",
      "score": 0.03059972506616878,
      "brand": "Google",
      "model": "Pixel 3",
      "rating": 3,
      "timestamp": "2021-08-15",
